& [MethodologicalFault] limits those aggregate positive metrics
  + [frozen_schema] permits subject enum cantor for all three procedures
  + [corpus_fault] twenty-five positive cases expected Weaver, Honesty, Security, Observer, Planner, Scribe, or Refiner even though profile 0.1 does not admit those subjects
  + [supported_positive_cases] are only five cases whose expected subject is cantor
  + [supported_positive_result] is one exact resolution and four fail-closed refusals
  + [conclusion] the raw 1 of 30 exact score and 14 of 30 procedure score are archived measurements but are not valid general positive-accuracy estimates for the frozen contract domain

& [RuntimeGroundingFault] is independently material
  + [out_of_domain_admissions] thirteen of the twenty-five unsupported-subject cases selected the expected procedure above threshold
  + [forced_argument] every admitted case carried subject cantor because the registered schema enum allowed only cantor
  + [stimulus_conflict] those thirteen stimuli named another faculty and did not name Cantor as their requested subject
  + [host_gap] select_procedure validates the schema and trusts Needle's optional grounding account but does not deterministically require extracted identity-bearing strings to occur in the caller stimulus
  + [containment] route-only mode stopped before Cantor query and llama.cpp articulation, so no wrong-subject semantic answer was produced in this calibration
  + [risk] the same selection in a full run could resolve Cantor while the caller requested a different subject

& [ReliableFindings] survive the methodology fault
  + all six negative controls refused without an admitted procedure
  + no prompt selected a different procedure than the intended positive family
  + explicit, key-value, JSON-like, and line-field forms commonly selected identity and transition procedures above the 0.65 gate
  + selected argument confidence was high while subject identity was wrong, proving confidence cannot substitute for deterministic grounding
  + all thirty-six route records were published and the aggregate evidence independently reverified

& [RequiredCorrection] is source-first
  + add a host-side caller-stimulus grounding predicate after typed schema validation and before procedure admission
  + reject any identity-bearing or caller-attributed string argument absent from normalized caller stimulus
  + bind future calibration expectations to the frozen procedure input schemas before first execution
  + use only subject cantor in a corrected profile 0.1 in-domain corpus
  + preserve this corpus and evidence unchanged as evaluation history
